  "title": "Intraday Drawdowns",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "63d04125-c655-4503-b68d-c31f137e500d",
      "question": "Among the 50 most liquid US stocks, which 10 sessions from February 2 through February 27, 2026 had the deepest drawdowns from the session's running high, and how did each one close relative to its open?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T18:54:12.351973Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T18:54:29.109803Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Top 10 deepest intraday drawdowns among the 50 most liquid US stocks, February 2–27, 2026**\n\n| Rank | Ticker | Session | Max Drawdown | Open → Close Return | Open | High | Low | Close | Volume |\n|------|--------|---------|--------------|---------------------|------|------|-----|-------|--------|\n| 1 | BMNR | 2026-02-05 | −13.89% | −9.61% | $19.25 | $20.07 | $17.19 | $17.40 | 62.6M |\n| 2 | IBM | 2026-02-23 | −13.28% | −12.21% | $254.37 | $255.19 | $220.72 | $223.30 | 16.4M |\n| 3 | CRWV | 2026-02-04 | −11.57% | −7.76% | $89.55 | $91.95 | $81.01 | $82.60 | 18.7M |\n| 4 | COIN | 2026-02-05 | −11.47% | −9.13% | $160.60 | $165.00 | $145.16 | $145.93 | 23.7M |\n| 5 | MU | 2026-02-04 | −11.39% | −8.02% | $410.59 | $413.00 | $363.90 | $377.65 | 40.5M |\n| 6 | CRWD | 2026-02-20 | −10.23% | −7.20% | $419.11 | $431.88 | $387.11 | $388.95 | 6.8M |\n| 7 | CRWV | 2026-02-27 | −10.09% | −5.62% | $84.22 | $84.38 | $75.66 | $79.49 | 49.7M |\n| 8 | AMAT | 2026-02-04 | −10.05% | −9.81% | $323.78 | $323.99 | $287.49 | $292.03 | 9.6M |\n| 9 | CRWD | 2026-02-05 | −9.59% | −9.11% | $414.80 | $416.29 | $374.52 | $377.02 | 4.6M |\n| 10 | CRWV | 2026-02-05 | −9.55% | −6.28% | $79.65 | $81.97 | $73.75 | $74.65 | 16.7M |\n\n**Notes**\n- *Max Drawdown* is the deepest peak-to-trough fall during the regular session, measured from the session’s running high (negative values shown as percentages).\n- *Open → Close Return* is the session’s return from the opening price to the closing price.\n- The scan covered all 50 most-liquid stocks (`top_50` universe) across 19 trading sessions (950 asset-sessions) from 2026-02-02 through 2026-02-27.\n- CRWV appears three times in the top 10 (Feb 4, 5, and 27), and CRWD appears twice (Feb 5 and 20).\n- All figures are from regular-session minute bars; the `max_drawdown` metric is negative by construction (a fall from the high).\n\n[1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — intraday scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:b7d136970aca64b55d1c39e7e817622ef8b4f531914ff740e5b1b0be1a6c8c45`",
